  "description": "ZICXAO crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H82 Gd4 Mn4 N10 O44,4(C3 H7 N1 O1),C6 H15 N1,16(C1 H4 O1),H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.632-3.997 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 99.25-122.57°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H82Gd4Mn4N10O44·4(C3H7NO)·C6H15N·16(CH4O)·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
